    {
      "disposition": "resolved",
      "id": "N40V7-F13",
      "severity": "critical",
      "summary": "The second of two independent, concurrent defects surfaced by this round's N70 live production run (the first is N30V7-F05, filed alongside this finding): the same missing-terminal_candidate gap `_boundary` had (N40V7-F12, fixed earlier this lineage), one layer further in. `deterministic_node` (nodes/__init__.py) catches `ExpectedFailure` itself -- before an exception ever reaches graph.py's `_boundary` -- and had the identical bug: its except-block returned `{pending_failure, pending_guard: None}` with no `terminal_candidate`, so `_failure_destination` (routing.py) routed straight to D98_WRITE_TERMINAL (no classifier hop for a deterministic node's failure, unlike a model node's, which D91 shapes first) and D98's independent revalidation rejected the bare `None` candidate as 'not a JSON object' -- discarding the real, already-classified failure (this run: D06B's SystemFailure over the N30V7-F05 locator bug) into the same uninformative generic rejection this whole finding lineage keeps tracing back to. `nodes/__init__.py` was not previously covered by any node's write set -- amended N40_INTEGRATION_OWNERSHIP's `writes:` list in implementation.graph.v7.yaml to add it (the same architectural boundary concern as the already-owned graph.py, one layer inward). Fixed: the except-block now also builds a SYSTEM_FAILURE-shaped `terminal_candidate` (kind/failure/node/safe_heads/audit_high_water_mark) from the caught error's own `failure_class`/`cause`, matching every other SYSTEM_FAILURE writer's shape exactly, using the full incoming `state` (available before `project()` narrows it) for `artifact_heads`/`evidence_index_entries`. New regression test drives `deterministic_node` directly with a body that raises `SystemFailure`, proving the synthesized candidate is accepted by the real `validate_terminal_candidate`. One existing test (`test_d30_refuses_to_pause_on_a_non_pause_failure`, N30-owned) asserted the absence of `terminal_candidate` -- encoding the very bug being fixed -- corrected to assert its presence and validity instead. Full N40 suite: 210 passed (up from 209, +1 for the new deterministic_node regression test), zero scan violations (11 files now scanned, up from 10), 75/75 ownership claims valid."
    }
  ],
